<Sequence DisplayName="Reminder Bot - Main" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_28">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>REMINDER BOT — implements docs/phase2/bot_reminder.md.

Trigger: Orchestrator time trigger, cron 0 0,30 7-21 * * ?, Asia/Kolkata,
max concurrent jobs 1, stop if running longer than 20 minutes.

Build the activity tree inside each stage. The stage order is the design.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<Sequence.Variables>
<Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtDue" />
<Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtDue24" />
<Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtDue2" />
<Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtRules" />
<Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtTemplates" />
<Variable x:TypeArguments="scg:Dictionary(x:String, x:Object)" Name="Config" />
</Sequence.Variables>
<ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log - Start" Level="Info" Message='["ReminderBot starting. DryRun=" &amp; in_DryRun.ToString()]' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_17" />
<Sequence DisplayName="1. Initialisation" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_19">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Load Data/Config.xlsx, Data/rules.xlsx and Data/templates.xlsx.
Get Orchestrator assets. A missing credential is a SYSTEM exception: stop the job.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke InitAllSettings.xaml ; Get Assets HMS_BaseUrl, HMS_ApiKey, Twilio_*, SendGrid_*" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_18" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="2. Quiet hours gate" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_21">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Never message a patient between 21:00 and 07:00.
Policy is DEFER, not DROP: a 2h reminder due at 06:00 is picked up by the 07:00
run and still arrives an hour before the appointment. An appointment that has
already started is logged SKIPPED / TOO_LATE.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): If Now outside rules reminders.quiet_hours (07:00-21:00) -&gt; log and end" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_20" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="3. Fetch due reminders" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_24">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Time-triggered, not queue-driven: an appointment becomes due because time passed,
not because an event fired.

The HMS applies the window tolerance (plus or minus 15 minutes around T-24h and
T-2h), excludes cancelled appointments and anything already SENT, and skips the
24h reminder for late bookings made inside 2 hours.
in_NowOverride, when set, is passed as &amp;now= so tests can time-travel.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): HTTP GET /api/v1/reminders/due?window=24H -&gt; dtDue24" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_22" />
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): HTTP GET /api/v1/reminders/due?window=2H  -&gt; dtDue2" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_23" />
</Sequence>
<ui:ForEachRow DisplayName="4. For each due appointment" DataTable="[dtDue]" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="ForEachRow_25">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Trigger setting Max concurrent jobs = 1 is load-bearing. The idempotency check
covers re-runs, but two runs racing on the same appointment could both pass the
check before either writes its notification row.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:ForEachRow.Body>
<ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="sd:DataRow">
<ActivityAction.Argument><DelegateInArgument x:TypeArguments="sd:DataRow" Name="row" /></ActivityAction.Argument>
<Sequence DisplayName="Handle one appointment" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_16">
<Sequence DisplayName="A. Idempotency check" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_2">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Before anything else: has a SENT notification of this type already been logged?
  GET /api/v1/notifications?appointment_id={id}&amp;type={REMINDER_24H|REMINDER_2H}&amp;status=SENT
Found -&gt; log SKIPPED / DUPLICATE, increment out_Skipped, move to the next row.

This check is what makes the bot safe to run twice. The trigger can double-fire,
a run can crash half way; running five times must send exactly what one run sends.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): GET /api/v1/notifications?appointment_id=&amp;type= ; skip if status SENT" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_1" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="B. Resolve channel" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_4">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/ResolveChannel.xaml — PURE LOGIC, NO I/O. Unit-testable.

Neither consent                         -&gt; SKIPPED / NO_CONSENT
preferred_channel = SMS   : SMS, fall back to EMAIL
preferred_channel = EMAIL : EMAIL, fall back to SMS
preferred_channel = BOTH  : every available channel
Phone must match ^\+[1-9]\d{9,14}$ ; email must be present.
Nothing usable                          -&gt; SKIPPED / NO_CHANNEL

Escalation: REMINDER_2H for URGENT or HIGH priority ignores the preference and
sends on every consented channel. Missing an urgent appointment costs more
than a redundant message.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke Workflows/ResolveChannel.xaml -&gt; channels list or skip reason" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_3" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="C. Render template" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_6">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Data/templates.xlsx keyed by template_id, e.g. TPL_REMINDER_24H_EN.
Placeholders: {PatientName} {DoctorName} {Department} {Date} {Time} {ReferenceNo} {HospitalName}
SMS body must stay at or under 160 characters after substitution — 161 is two
billed Twilio segments.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke Workflows/RenderTemplate.xaml" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_5" />
</Sequence>
<TryCatch DisplayName="D. Send with retry" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_12">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Retries happen INSIDE this run, never deferred to the next trigger — the next
trigger may be 30 minutes away and a 2h reminder cannot wait that long.

Attempt 1 at 0s, attempt 2 after 5s, attempt 3 after 15s.
Retryable:     HTTP 429, 500, 502, 503, 504, network timeout
Not retryable: Twilio 21211 (bad number), 21608 (unverified on trial),
               21610 (unsubscribed), SendGrid 400, any 401

Twilio 21610 is the one case this bot writes patient data:
  PATCH /api/v1/patients/{id} {"sms_consent": false}

in_DryRun = True -&gt; do not call the gateway; record provider = DRYRUN.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<TryCatch.Try>
<Sequence DisplayName="Send" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_8">
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke Workflows/SendWithRetry.xaml -&gt; shared/SendSMS.xaml or shared/SendEmail.xaml" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_7" />
</Sequence>
</TryCatch.Try>
<TryCatch.Catches>
<Catch x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Catch_13">
<ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="s:Exception">
<ActivityAction.Argument><DelegateInArgument x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" Name="ex" /></ActivityAction.Argument>
<Sequence DisplayName="Send failed after retries" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_11">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Exhausted retries: log a FAILED notification with the gateway error code, raise a
LOW conflict so someone fixes the contact data, and CONTINUE. One patient's bad
phone number must not stop the other reminders in this run.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log send failure" Level="Warn" Message='["Reminder failed: " &amp; ex.Message]' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_9" />
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): POST /api/v1/notifications status FAILED ; POST /api/v1/conflicts severity LOW ; continue to next row" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_10" />
</Sequence>
</ActivityAction>
</Catch>
</TryCatch.Catches>
</TryCatch>
